==============================================================================
PARITY — every web UserCell branch reproduced (no scope narrowing)
==============================================================================
- The web cell renders exactly two branches; both are reproduced and neither is hidden:
  * EMPTY  : `!user || (!user.name && !user.email && !user.id)` (untrimmed JS truthiness) ->
             a muted em-dash "—" (web `data-testid="user-cell-empty"`,
             `text-[var(--text-muted)]`) -> native UserCellEmpty (Color.TS.textMuted).
  * POPULATED: the composed Avatar (size=size, showTooltip=ALWAYS true) + the display name
             (text-sm / --text-primary / truncate -> Font.TS.body + Color.TS.textPrimary +
             lineLimit(1).tail) and, only when `showEmail && user.email`, a muted email line
             beneath (text-xs / --text-muted / truncate -> Font.TS.bodySm + Color.TS.textMuted).
- Display-name priority chain ported verbatim: `name.trim() || email.split('@')[0] || id ||
  t('avatar.unknown')`. Pinned in tests: name "Alice Adams" -> "Alice Adams"; "  Alice Adams  "
  -> trimmed; email-only "jane.smith@example.com" -> "jane.smith"; id-only "subject-abc" ->
  "subject-abc"; "@example.com"+id -> falls through to id; whitespace-only name + no other
  signal -> localised "Unknown user".
- The avatar is fed name=displayName and userId=user.id (web `userId={user.id} name={displayName}
  src={user.avatarUrl} showTooltip`), so initials/seed/colour derive from the SAME displayName the
  cell shows. Tie-tested: displayName "Alice Adams" -> AvatarIdentity.initials == "AA".
- showEmail default false (email hidden by default — web test "does NOT render the email by
  default"); when on with an empty address, no email line (the address is JS-falsy).
- size token (xs/sm/md/lg, default sm) carried to the avatar; avatarUrl carried to the avatar
  image. The web `className` prop is a styling hook with no native analogue (documented in source).

==============================================================================
STATES — every state the web source actually has is rendered
==============================================================================
- empty     : rendered (the muted em-dash; keeps dense tables scannable).
- populated : rendered (avatar + name + optional email).
- The web UserCell is a PURE presentational cell whose only data source is `useTranslation`
  (no query hook). It therefore has no network freshness axis — fabricating loading / error /
  stale / offline chips here would be DRIFT, not parity (Honesty Covenant #5 "no parity
  shortcuts", #9 "no silent drift"). This is the same disposition the Avatar surface (0076) took
  for the identical reason. The only genuine fetch in the cell is the avatar's optional remote
  image, whose loading/loaded/failed lifecycle is handled inside the composed Avatar (AsyncImage
  -> fallback disc), so the cell is never a blank box.

i18n (P1/S10)  : the one web key `avatar.unknown` ("Unknown user") resolves through the
  NSLocalizedString facade (UserCellStrings, table "UserCell"); shipped in UserCell.strings; no
  English literals in the Swift sources. Verified at runtime via the injected-resolver test
  (custom resolver -> "Inconnu").
a11y           : the cell folds into ONE VoiceOver element (children: .ignore) — label = display
  name (or the em-dash), value = email when shown — so the name is not voiced twice (avatar +
  label). Dynamic Type respected via Font.TS tokens; Reduce-Motion respected by the composed
  Avatar's image cross-fade. No interactive elements in this cell (display-only).
telemetry (P1/S11): UserCellModel emits `view.opened` exactly once with slug "UserCell"
  (asserted: not re-emitted after stop/start).
state-holder (P1/S8): the view binds through UserCellModel over a UserCellSource seam
  (LiveUserCellSource in production, InMemoryUserCellSource in tests/previews); no HTTP in the view.

